                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1e6f37b1-c07f-31f2-95ce-80fe1bbc5136",
                        "entry_id": "74c60596-117c-3760-962f-fd223fd9b38d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар., прост. то, что затрудняет, суета, беспокойство, хлопоты; то же, что колготня"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "67d6451b-c7e5-4c2c-9491-a934abe3c7df",
                                "sense_id": "1e6f37b1-c07f-31f2-95ce-80fe1bbc5136",
                                "text": "А теперь, как царь на войну разохотился, во все стороны рукой достал, мужиков на свое дело собрал, еще невиданная колгота пошла."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8fc204a8-d34a-4714-9023-d14ceb4f842e",
                        "source_entry_id": "74c60596-117c-3760-962f-fd223fd9b38d",
                        "source_sense_id": "1e6f37b1-c07f-31f2-95ce-80fe1bbc5136",
                        "target_lang_word": "fuss",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fuss",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "66bce4ea-d562-3a62-8bfa-66ac190b1d10",
                                        "entry_id": "f667c975-b116-38e7-ada6-78ca63903fd1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Excessive activity, worry, bother, or talk about something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "676b296a-8496-48cf-84a5-fe234e6e5ff4",
                                                "sense_id": "66bce4ea-d562-3a62-8bfa-66ac190b1d10",
                                                "text": "They made a big fuss about the wedding plans."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02b41447-ebaa-46d8-85f9-afc5e82bd71d",
                                                "sense_id": "66bce4ea-d562-3a62-8bfa-66ac190b1d10",
                                                "text": "What's all the fuss about?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1419121-d9ca-4b22-a059-ac83f79bf8e4",
                                                "sense_id": "66bce4ea-d562-3a62-8bfa-66ac190b1d10",
                                                "text": "Sickness did not last above a ten days; my poor wife zealously assiduous, and with a minimum of fuss or noise."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3fcd38e-98fb-4572-ab17-82aed8b3656e",
                                                "sense_id": "66bce4ea-d562-3a62-8bfa-66ac190b1d10",
                                                "text": "“Anthea hasn't a notion in her head but to vamp a lot of silly mugwumps. She's set her heart on that tennis bloke[…]whom the papers are making such a fuss about.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0564d516-79ea-4755-a82e-3b7e0b4761a8",
                                                "sense_id": "66bce4ea-d562-3a62-8bfa-66ac190b1d10",
                                                "text": "But in the reader comments section beneath the FT piece, many couldn’t understand what all the fuss was about. “I’m surprised to see the FT reporting this sort of thing,” one person wrote."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1316775d-0d76-39ed-9e33-667951302405",
                                        "entry_id": "f667c975-b116-38e7-ada6-78ca63903fd1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A complaint or noise; a scene."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b060867-8f98-4bef-a8b4-e16d5ed6ab82",
                                                "sense_id": "1316775d-0d76-39ed-9e33-667951302405",
                                                "text": "If you make enough of a fuss about the problem, maybe they'll fix it for you."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "46c0fad0-e85d-3557-a8c3-27679a23b5dd",
                                        "entry_id": "f667c975-b116-38e7-ada6-78ca63903fd1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An exhibition of affection or admiration."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af648191-e585-47cb-aefc-8f50f707fa5e",
                                                "sense_id": "46c0fad0-e85d-3557-a8c3-27679a23b5dd",
                                                "text": "They made a great fuss over the new baby."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "fuss",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "035dd445-9847-32f5-8863-8881cbcab842",
                                        "entry_id": "dbf56873-24ab-3c30-968f-abdc7cebcf04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be very worried or excited about something, often too much."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7855fbb-09d3-4e02-9016-9cb7d6e48424",
                                                "sense_id": "035dd445-9847-32f5-8863-8881cbcab842",
                                                "text": "His grandmother will never quit fussing over his vegetarianism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "108d311a-8c7d-4e1b-9371-2ae4e6caf13b",
                                                "sense_id": "035dd445-9847-32f5-8863-8881cbcab842",
                                                "text": "Dear reader, spare me. I don't hate men, I love them; I eat 'em for breakfast. But it seems to me that fussing about masculinity is intimately related to homophobia."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d48dc032-5d36-3ec0-80f1-f1df243afe31",
                                        "entry_id": "dbf56873-24ab-3c30-968f-abdc7cebcf04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To fiddle; fidget; wiggle, or adjust"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f238fdd1-17a2-4573-874c-55b094e7f28d",
                                                "sense_id": "d48dc032-5d36-3ec0-80f1-f1df243afe31",
                                                "text": "Quit fussing with your hair. It looks fine."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2b22380d-0ff2-32e8-876a-5ca60064428a",
                                        "entry_id": "dbf56873-24ab-3c30-968f-abdc7cebcf04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To disturb (a person)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1edbf749-f840-3c79-bd53-e489b8344a51",
                                        "entry_id": "dbf56873-24ab-3c30-968f-abdc7cebcf04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cry or be ill-humoured."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "especially",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d072b864-e8ca-3c61-b489-47aabb3d3587",
                                        "entry_id": "dbf56873-24ab-3c30-968f-abdc7cebcf04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To show affection for, especially animals."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3d6a9f07-37b0-38b6-a8aa-5380d0f0d420",
                                        "entry_id": "dbf56873-24ab-3c30-968f-abdc7cebcf04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To pet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8dec1747-3971-4fa6-b4a5-0b019b78a969",
                                                "sense_id": "3d6a9f07-37b0-38b6-a8aa-5380d0f0d420",
                                                "text": "He fussed the cat."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9db75371-40bf-42b4-ac3c-7837309f9d5c",
                        "source_entry_id": "74c60596-117c-3760-962f-fd223fd9b38d",
                        "source_sense_id": "1e6f37b1-c07f-31f2-95ce-80fe1bbc5136",
                        "target_lang_word": "bustle",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bustle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0718f116-0f01-3537-9f7c-f37bd1a29242",
                                        "entry_id": "3c44ada7-2d2c-3c19-b1ad-d92f3260b2aa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An excited activity; a stir."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26b20fba-a7c8-497b-8aee-733746e4e294",
                                                "sense_id": "0718f116-0f01-3537-9f7c-f37bd1a29242",
                                                "text": "In the midſt of all this buſtle, I was ſtruck with the appearance of a large bevy of beauties and women of the firſt fashion, who with all the perfect confidence of good breeding, inſhrined themſelves in the ſeveral temples dedicated to the Cyprian Venus[.]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83947a97-bb0d-4741-b86a-bfc760fbcb45",
                                                "sense_id": "0718f116-0f01-3537-9f7c-f37bd1a29242",
                                                "text": "we are, perhaps, all the while flattering our natural indolence, which, hating the bustle of the world, and drudgery of business seeks a pretence of reason to give itself a full and uncontrolled indulgence."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6681b38a-a822-3b3e-a584-3c40c3358e00",
                                        "entry_id": "3c44ada7-2d2c-3c19-b1ad-d92f3260b2aa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cover to protect and hide the back panel of a computer or other office machine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9268e8b4-497a-3090-a54e-13bad678d693",
                                        "entry_id": "3c44ada7-2d2c-3c19-b1ad-d92f3260b2aa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A frame worn underneath a woman's skirt, typically only protruding from the rear as opposed to the earlier more circular hoops."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc9a110b-58eb-4fb4-ab23-eda944c5eaed",
                                                "sense_id": "9268e8b4-497a-3090-a54e-13bad678d693",
                                                "text": "All the portraits that hang on the walls of the living room are, I realize, of my mother's family: miniatures of her great-aunts in Victorian bustles and elaborate feathered hats; a gilt-framed oil of her great-great-great-uncle as a boy in pastoral England, wearing a gold riding coat over white jodhpurs and sitting astride a white steed, a King Charles spaniel yapping at them from the foreground of the canvas."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "bustle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "790072e6-a4cc-3786-bffd-f6e756b1c6f2",
                                        "entry_id": "20ad084f-ca1d-3973-9ca0-c143971c0f3f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To move busily and energetically with fussiness (often followed by about)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c341664-d506-4ea4-8af5-c00eecea49d2",
                                                "sense_id": "790072e6-a4cc-3786-bffd-f6e756b1c6f2",
                                                "text": "The commuters bustled about inside the train station."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61196184-155b-4e59-ade5-b2baec05a93d",
                                                "sense_id": "790072e6-a4cc-3786-bffd-f6e756b1c6f2",
                                                "text": "I was once so mad to bussell abroad, and seek about for preferment […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e427dae0-b605-392e-abbf-d4682ebe7455",
                                        "entry_id": "20ad084f-ca1d-3973-9ca0-c143971c0f3f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To teem or abound (usually followed by with); to exhibit an energetic and active abundance (of a thing)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f874ee3-cdbd-4fbe-8a9f-11767b692fe3",
                                                "sense_id": "e427dae0-b605-392e-abbf-d4682ebe7455",
                                                "text": "The train station was bustling with commuters."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d91af679-37f3-3d90-be43-ba54606a8b84",
                                        "entry_id": "20ad084f-ca1d-3973-9ca0-c143971c0f3f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To push around, to importune."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57a89d1d-f98f-4597-83bd-203a1b556dbc",
                                                "sense_id": "d91af679-37f3-3d90-be43-ba54606a8b84",
                                                "text": "Don’t bustle her or fuss or snatch: / A suitor looking at his watch / Is not a posture that persuades / Willing, much less reluctant maids."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
